Description: Linux UEFI boot toolkit: diagnose, repair, migrate
 lamboot-tools is a CLI suite for diagnosing, repairing, migrating, and
 maintaining UEFI boot configurations on Linux. It treats GRUB, systemd-boot,
 rEFInd, Limine, and LamBoot as first-class peers and works on any UEFI system
 regardless of the installed bootloader.
 .
 Tools: lamboot-diagnose (boot-chain scanner), lamboot-esp (ESP health and
 cleanup), lamboot-backup (boot-config snapshot/restore), lamboot-repair
 (online and offline repair), lamboot-migrate (BIOS to UEFI conversion),
 lamboot-doctor (guided diagnose-repair-verify), lamboot-uki-build (Unified
 Kernel Image builder), lamboot-signing-keys (Secure Boot key lifecycle),
 lamboot-toolkit (suite dispatcher), and lamboot-inspect (LamBoot deep
 introspection, Python). Every tool emits structured JSON on a stable schema.
 .
 This package bundles the prebuilt, statically linked component binaries
 lamboot-capcheck (firmware and platform capability auditor) and lamboot-reader
 (GRUB configuration reader). Because of those bundled binaries this package is
 distributed from the Lamco apt repository only; it is not eligible for Debian
 main, which requires building all binaries from source.
